      "question": "Why did the authors choose self-attention over recurrent layers?",
      "expected": "complexity, parallelization, path length",
      "answer": "Based on the context provided, the authors chose self-attention over recurrent layers for the following reasons:\n\n1.  **Computational Complexity and Speed:** Self-attention layers connect all positions with a constant number of sequentially executed operations ($O(1)$), whereas recurrent layers require $O(n)$ sequential operations. Consequently, self-attention layers are faster than recurrent layers when the sequence length is small.\n2.  **Interpretability:** Self-attention can yield more interpretable models. The authors observed that individual attention heads clearly learned to perform different tasks and exhibited behavior related to the syntactic and semantic structure of sentences.",
